{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: All scvi_n200 + vit_l + multiprofile combinations (transformer/avgpool × weighted/concat) have been tested, with config_025 (transformer, weighted) as the best at 0.725. The remaining untested dimensions are the RNA encoder (pca_n2000, scgpt) and image encoder (resnet50). scgpt has already shown to be poor (0.507), and resnet50 underperformed vit_l (0.713 vs 0.725). This experiment tests pca_n2000 with the best aggregation/fusion setting (transformer + weighted) and the best image encoder (vit_l), directly probing whether a simpler linear RNA encoder can match the learned scvi_n200 encoder in the optimal multimodal pipeline. This is the best use of experiment 8 because: (1) it reduces uncertainty about the most important remaining design choice (RNA encoder) in the highest-performing configuration space, (2) if pca_n2000 performs comparably, it offers a significantly cheaper alternative for deployment, and (3) if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential, allowing the final 2 experiments to focus on fine-tuning the resnet50/vit_l trade-off or accepting config_025 as the optimum. Expected relative cost: moderate (~3–4 GPU hours), slightly cheaper than config_025 (3.60 h) since PCA encoding is a fast linear projection versus scvi's iterative VAE training, while the ViT-L and transformer aggregation dominate runtime."
}

